so  [Music]  [Music]  in my last video i was doing my best to  slow down in santa fe new mexico  in reality i spent most of my time  organizing the van preparing taxes and  finishing up some photography work  when the time finally came to relax  nathaniel and i were pitched a  last-minute job by mazda to shoot the  new cx-50 in santa barbara california  the offer was too good to pass up so  before we knew it we were back on the  west coast making our way south from los  angeles to the hotel california in santa  barbara california  this is home sweet home for the next  couple days  so beautiful  this trip to california was more than a  month ago and i've filmed two or three  new videos since then  it's been interesting sharing my life in  such a delayed and public way  when i sit down to edit i'm usually  looking at six to eight weeks of footage  very little which makes any sense when  dropped together into a timeline  different days different moods different  places a sunset here dinner there  i watch each clip one by one wondering  what is the story here  is there a story  sometimes there is and sometimes there  isn't  it's 10 p.m  tomorrow's kind of a full day because  we're gonna go shooting and then we have  a mountain biking event which we're  doing as a group and then we have a big  group dinner so  yeah it's going to be pretty full on and  this  shower is  definitely nicer than what i have in my  van which is nothing so  so  [Music]  [Music]  cheers  out  let's go  it's 5 16 a.m  we're a little bit behind but uh  i think we're gonna make it up for  sunrise no problem  [Music]  sound gets in your bones  everybody driving under  love's not a destination  i think it's a journey home  so what if mine is on the lonely road  what  [Music]  that's the sound of my one and only in  the distance  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  all right first light has hit  and we just shot some layers out there  getting a shot  back to the old horizon  influencers in the wild  [Music]  we just ordered room service and we're  taking some story content because it's  all part of the experience  look at that toast i'm so excited to eat  this some bts of  what we do  [Music]  my mind tends to wander to whatever's  right in front of me and whatever's  happening right now  so sometimes i struggle when creating  these videos  [Music]  and pretending to be present a moment  that's already passed  but it's also teaching me to be patient  to reflect and take note of all the  beautiful roads this life has led me  down  [Music]  [Applause]  as i'm editing this video i'm actually  camped out in utah in the middle of  nowhere  the irony of editing this footage of  cocktail parties rooftop dinners and  nights spent in an 800 hotel room all  while actually sitting in the middle of  the desert  hot sweaty going on day six without a  shower and wearing the same dirty  clothes i've worn literally for the past  three days  sometimes it feels like i'm living a  double life  always existing at the extreme end of  things  from sleeping in the back of my suv to  house-sitting million-dollar homes from  living on room service and five-star  hotels to sleeping in the backcountry  and cooking stale ramen we made it  into the car  that was a whirlwind of packing and  running  no more room service for us  i like to think the constant change  keeps me flexible and open-minded  but  i don't really know if nothing else one  thing is for sure  it's always an adventure and pretty much  never boring  [Music]  we had a lot of editing to do for the  monster project so we booked an airbnb  out near the mountains and  stayed still for a few days while a big  storm rolled through  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  taos reminded me of just how much i love  thunderstorms  especially in the mountains  the sense of rain  the warm wind the way the light dances  with the dark  i was reminded of when i was little and  dreamed of being a storm chaser  who knows  maybe i still do  [Music]  later that week we met up with some  friends in taos and spent a few days  catching up that's pretty cool  we're just outside of taos and we're  doing hike  through some hot springs  with nathaniel ann and clint  let's say it's high free eye  this place is beautiful  [Music]  you know the polaris  [Music]  the coolest thing  [Music]  mariah nate and i camped out in the  house together for a few days and i  filmed absolutely nothing  except for a few short clips here and  there we spent most of our time just  hanging out living life  after a few shared campfires some deep  talks and really long walks we set our  see you laters and headed back out onto  the road  so  [Music]  [Music]  so  [Music]  holy crap is so windy  i am fighting to keep my  van in between the lines here this road  is crappy  and the wind is intense  and it's been like this for the past  i don't know  hour and a half  what  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  and this is where i'll leave you  parked on a cliff edge in the middle of  the windstorm  heading in tonight  i'll see you next time  thanks for being here

